    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d981">

                <pb facs="1123" n="1043" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1043"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 228.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with the Department’s No. 216
                    of the 16th instant in regard to the protection of American interests at Bitlis
                    by the British vice-consul there, I have to acknowledge the receipt of your No.
                    237 of the 24th ultimo.</p>
                <p>The Department will be pleased to have you apply to, the British ambassador at
                    Constantinople for the necessary authorization for the vice-consul to use his
                    good offices for Americans in his jurisdiction, and to secure vizierial
                    directions sent to the governor-general at Bitlis to recognize such good
                    offices.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
